Date: Wed, 7 Oct 2026 01:38:58 +0700
Subject: [PATCH] SourbyCraft - reopen bridge admission when a plugin is
 enabled again

Disable closes a bridged plugin's admission. Enabling the same instance
again does not ask the loader, so admission stayed closed and every task
it scheduled was rejected. Before onEnable, re-open admission for a
plugin the bridge already admitted; native plugins and quarantine are
unaffected.

diff --git a/src/main/java/io/papermc/paper/plugin/manager/PaperPluginInstanceManager.java b/src/main/java/io/papermc/paper/plugin/manager/PaperPluginInstanceManager.java
index dc8c9b2433ace53521ef7b06a57ff7947ca92b0a..3fe582f6e8f89e3879d03662904ee11401f9bb98 100644
--- a/src/main/java/io/papermc/paper/plugin/manager/PaperPluginInstanceManager.java
+++ b/src/main/java/io/papermc/paper/plugin/manager/PaperPluginInstanceManager.java
@@ -197,6 +197,7 @@ class PaperPluginInstanceManager {
                 }
             } // Paper
 
+            dev.iyanz.sourbycraft.bridge.AuroraBridge.onPluginEnabled(plugin); // SourbyCraft - reopen bridge admission a previous disable closed
             try {
                 jPlugin.setEnabled(true);
             } catch (Throwable ex) {
